# Keep the build context small and keep CUDA out of the screening image.

# The training environment. Torch, torchvision, ultralytics - gigabytes, and
# every one of them a thing CLAUDE.md rule 2 says must not be in this process.
.venv-train/
.venv/
runs/
*.pt
weights/

# Datasets. `data/raw` and `data/processed` are hundreds of megabytes of
# training inputs the screening path never opens.
data/raw/
data/processed/
SIH/

# The archives those directories were unpacked from - 2.3 GB between them, and
# they were the single largest thing in the first image I built. `.gitignore`
# has excluded `*.zip` since the beginning; this file did not, and nothing
# warns you: the build simply succeeds and the image is a few gigabytes larger
# than it should be. Measure the image, do not assume the ignore file is
# complete.
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz

# The console has its own image and its own build context (`docker-compose.yml`,
# the `console` service). Nothing under `api/ core/ fusion/ modules/` reads it,
# so shipping the React tree inside the screening image serves nobody.
frontend/

# The build-time *dependency set*. Pillow and Faker never enter the screening
# image; only the code that would use them, and only because the test suite
# runs in the image (see the verify profile in docker-compose.yml) and
# tests/test_tamper.py imports data/tools/mutate.py.
#
# data/generator/ and data/tools/ therefore stay in the image while their
# dependencies do not - so the generator tests skip there rather than run, and
# nothing on the screening path can import a downloader. That last part is not
# a convention: tests/test_offline.py enforces it by walking the AST.
requirements-build.txt

# Runtime state. `var/` is a volume; baking a database into the image would
# ship one machine's screening history to every other machine.
var/
*.db

# Local noise.
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.playwright-mcp/
node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
infooo.pdf

# NOT ignored, deliberately:
#   models/     baked in - that is the offline claim (CLAUDE.md rule 3)
#   config/     profiles, weights, bands, the measured layout reference
#   profiles/   the six document profiles
#   tests/      so `docker compose run api pytest` can prove the image
